ligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $CD=DC={I}_{2}$\n- $DE=ED={I}_{2}$\n- $D={C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11637/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71818/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "aa714ee5-f884-54f4-ba5f-0e43ffcf59fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71818/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "07aee5fb-e365-5077-a44f-10c44eb69f67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71818/selection/df67a18079e3b